  <span class="eyebrow">Purpose &amp; practice</span><h2>Turning capability into opportunity.</h2>
  <p>I am a social entrepreneur, innovation strategist, and ecosystem builder focused on turning ideas, talent, and real-world challenges into sustainable enterprises and measurable impact.</p>
  <p>My work sits at the intersection of entrepreneurship, technology, education, sustainable development, and inclusive economic growth. I am particularly interested in building practical systems that help people and organisations move from learning and problem identification to validation, venture creation, market access, investment readiness, and long-term growth.</p>
  <p>A central part of my work is supporting entrepreneurs and innovators to develop solutions that are commercially viable, socially useful, and environmentally responsible. I believe entrepreneurship is most powerful when it creates opportunity, strengthens communities, and solves problems in ways that can endure beyond individual projects or funding cycles.</p>
  <h3>Connected interests. Practical outcomes.</h3>
  <p>My interests include social enterprise development, responsible innovation, digital platforms, renewable energy, regenerative agriculture, sustainable value chains, circular economy models, youth economic participation, market access, and impact investment. I am especially drawn to approaches that connect producers, entrepreneurs, institutions, investors, and markets through more transparent, accountable, and inclusive systems.</p>
  <p>I also work on the design of innovation ecosystems that combine applied learning, mentorship, enterprise development, research, technology, partnerships, and evidence. Rather than treating training, finance, incubation, and market access as separate interventions, I focus on how these elements can work together as a continuous pathway from capability to opportunity.</p>
  <h3>Locally grounded. Globally connected.</h3>
  <p>Africa presents enormous opportunities for locally grounded innovation. I am committed to strengthening the infrastructure that enables African entrepreneurs, creators, and institutions to build, compete, and collaborate globally while responding to local economic, social, and environmental priorities.</p>
  <p>My approach is grounded in collaboration, integrity, evidence, and long-term value creation. I believe meaningful innovation requires more than good ideas; it requires capable people, strong institutions, responsible technology, access to markets, and partnerships that align incentives around shared outcomes.</p>
  <p>I welcome conversations and collaborations around entrepreneurship, innovation, technology, sustainable development, investment, education, responsible value chains, and building solutions that create lasting economic and social value.</p>
